Summary: Rosetta 2: make it notice code written into another process
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
From: CrossOver 26.3.0 CW HACK 18947 (dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c)
Source: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz (sources/wine/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c)
CW-Hack: 18947
Upstream: no
Why: NtWriteVirtualMemory writes another process's memory with
 mach_vm_write from wineserver, and Rosetta doesn't notice code changed
 that way: the target keeps running its old translation. After the write,
 toggle the executable bit off and on from inside the target
 (NtProtectVirtualMemory on the process handle) so Rosetta retranslates.
 Armadillo, the DRM in Big Fish games, writes "jmp $" (EB FE) over its
 child's entry point, waits for the child to reach it, then writes the
 original bytes back; without this the child spins on the stale "jmp $"
 for ever and activation fails.
Programs: Big Fish games (Armadillo DRM): activation fails, as gmActivator's
 child spins for ever on a stale "jmp $"
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: its NtWriteVirtualMemory calls NtQueryVirtualMemory and
 NtProtectVirtualMemory twice after the server call (disassembly). The
 inventory missed it because it adds no strings of its own.
Applies to: wine 11.22 (macfixes, after 0042)
Status: confirmed 2026-11-15 by hand: toggling the entry page's protection
 inside a stuck gmActivator child (lldb, mprotect) let it continue exactly
 as on Sikarugir 10.0_8. Not yet built.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 9120052..cc52179 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6645,6 +6645,57 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtReadVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, const void *addr, void *buf
 }
 
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+static int is_apple_silicon(void)
+{
+    static int apple_silicon_status, did_check = 0;
+    if (!did_check)
+    {
+        /* returns 0 for native process or on error, 1 for translated */
+        int ret = 0;
+        size_t size = sizeof(ret);
+        if (sysctlbyname( "sysctl.proc_translated", &ret, &size, NULL, 0 ) == -1)
+            apple_silicon_status = 0;
+        else
+            apple_silicon_status = ret;
+
+        did_check = 1;
+    }
+
+    return apple_silicon_status;
+}
+
+/* CW HACK 18947
+ * If mach_vm_write() is used to modify code cross-process (which is how we implement
+ * NtWriteVirtualMemory), Rosetta won't notice the change and will execute the "old" code.
+ *
+ * To work around this, after the write completes,
+ * toggle the executable bit (from inside the target process) on/off for any executable
+ * pages that were modified, to force Rosetta to re-translate it.
+ */
+static void toggle_executable_pages_for_rosetta( HANDLE process, void *addr, SIZE_T size )
+{
+    MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION info;
+    NTSTATUS status;
+    SIZE_T ret;
+
+    if (!is_apple_silicon())
+        return;
+
+    status = NtQueryVirtualMemory( process, addr, MemoryBasicInformation, &info, sizeof(info), &ret );
+
+    if (!status && (info.AllocationProtect & 0xf0))
+    {
+        DWORD origprot, noexec;
+        noexec = info.AllocationProtect & ~0xf0;
+        if (!noexec) noexec = PAGE_NOACCESS;
+
+        NtProtectVirtualMemory( process, &addr, &size, noexec, &origprot );
+        NtProtectVirtualMemory( process, &addr, &size, origprot, &noexec );
+    }
+}
+#endif
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *             NtWriteVirtualMemory   (NTDLL.@)
  *             ZwWriteVirtualMemory   (NTDLL.@)
@@ -6665,6 +6716,10 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtWriteVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, void *addr, const void *bu
             size = reply->written;
         }
         SERVER_END_REQ;
+
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        toggle_executable_pages_for_rosetta( process, addr, size );
+#endif
     }
     else
     {
